The root cause is that only `POST /orders` (`routes/orders.js:6-12`) uses `req.user.accountId`; the `PATCH`/`DELETE` handlers were written as if `id` alone were sufficient, which is the actual IDOR — any authenticated user can currently update or delete any account/order by id.

Recommendation: one middleware in `app.js`, mounted *before* `sessionUser` (line 11), that logs on `res.on('finish')` rather than immediately:

```js
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const start = Date.now();
  res.on("finish", () => {
    console.log({
      method: req.method,
      path: req.path,
      status: res.statusCode,
