Registering it before `sessionUser` means it still fires for requests that get rejected with `401` inside `sessionUser` (line 10) — `next()` is called immediately here, so the middleware itself runs first, but the `finish` listener doesn't fire until the response actually completes, by which point `req.user` is populated if auth succeeded. That gives you one uniform log line per request instead of needing separate logging in each route file.

