Given this schema, the simplest implementation that fits the codebase's existing style (one query, through the existing `db.write` chokepoint, no new abstraction needed) is to make the key part of the `orders` row itself rather than standing up a separate idempotency-tracking table:

```sql
ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN idempotency_key TEXT;
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX orders_account_idempotency_key
  ON orders (account_id, idempotency_key)
  WHERE idempotency_key IS NOT NULL;
```

