- Treat "0 rows returned/affected" as a 404, not a silent success — right now `db.write` returns `res.rows[0]`, which is `undefined` if the WHERE clause matches nothing; without the `if (!row)` check the handler would return `undefined`/200 instead of signaling the mismatch.
